The nightly behaviour-check job, waiting for Jon's approval of the spending (roadmap step 26, Phase 5). Not applied:
.github/workflows/portable.yml has no such job. To turn it on, from the repo root: git apply bench/behaviour-nightly.patch

What it runs: bash bench/behaviour_checks.sh once a night (the workflow's existing 06:41 UTC schedule) and on
demand, never on a pull request or a push. On a fresh boat.dev 4-core Linux machine the same script took
10 minutes and passed (bench/session-cost/behaviour-boat-2026-11-07.txt).

Expected spend: GitHub bills nothing for standard GitHub-hosted runners in public repositories, and this
repository is public (docs.github.com/en/billing/concepts/product-billing/github-actions, read 2026-11-07).
It would use about 10 to 15 runner-minutes a night, about 300 to 450 a month, at $0. If the repository were
private, the same minutes on a 2-core Linux runner would be $0.006 a minute: about $1.80 to $2.70 a month.

diff --git a/.github/workflows/portable.yml b/.github/workflows/portable.yml
index 055736c..a0b88bd 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/portable.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/portable.yml
@@ -290,6 +290,21 @@ jobs:
